Ladybird matches a content script’s include and exclude globs against
the whole serialized URL, with * for any run of characters and ? for
one, and matches an about:, data:, or blob: document as its creator’s
origin for a script with matchOriginAsFallback. Firefox does both in
MozDocumentMatcher::Matches() and MatchesURI() (WebExtensionPolicy.cpp),
with its MatchGlob for the globs. Chromium has no include or exclude
globs for registered scripts, but matches by origin for
match_origin_as_fallback the same way, and WebKit has neither.
